1
00:04:16,363 --> 00:04:22,363
They took his daughter. He'll take their lives.

2
00:08:32,727 --> 00:08:38,727
Taken is a action, thriller film directed by Pierre Morel.

3
00:12:49,090 --> 00:12:55,090
Bryan Mills, a former government operative, is trying to
reconnect with his teenage daughter Kim.

4
00:17:05,454 --> 00:17:11,454
After reluctantly agreeing with his ex-wife to let Kim go to Paris on
vacation with a friend, his worst nightmare comes true.

5
00:21:21,818 --> 00:21:27,818
While on the phone with his daughter shortly after she arrives in Paris, she
and her friend are abducted by a gang of human traffickers.

6
00:25:38,181 --> 00:25:44,181
Working against the clock, Bryan relies on his extensive training and skills to track down the
ruthless gang that abducted her and launch a one-man war to rescue his daughter.

7
00:29:54,545 --> 00:30:00,545
Bryan Mills, played by Liam Neeson.

8
00:34:10,909 --> 00:34:16,909
Kim Mills, played by Maggie Grace.

9
00:38:27,272 --> 00:38:33,272
Lenore St. John, played by Famke Janssen.

10
00:42:43,636 --> 00:42:49,636
Jean-Claude Pitrel, played by Olivier Rabourdin.

11
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Sam Gilroy, played by Leland Orser.

12
00:51:16,363 --> 00:51:22,363
Mark Casey, played by Jon Gries.

13
00:55:32,727 --> 00:55:38,727
Taken is a 2008 English-language French action-thriller film directed by
Pierre Morel and written by Luc Besson and Robert Mark Kamen.

14
00:59:49,090 --> 00:59:55,090
It stars Liam Neeson, Maggie Grace, Leland Orser, Jon Gries, David
Warshofsky, Katie Cassidy, Holly Valance and Famke Janssen.

15
01:04:05,454 --> 01:04:11,454
In the film, Bryan Mills, an ex-CIA officer, sets out to track down his teenage daughter Kim and her best
friend Amanda after they are kidnapped by Albanian human traffickers  while on vacation in France.

16
01:08:21,818 --> 01:08:27,818
Taken was released in France on February 27, 2008.

17
01:12:38,181 --> 01:12:44,181
The film received mixed reviews from critics, and was a financial
success, grossing $226 million against a $25 million budget.

18
01:16:54,545 --> 01:17:00,545
Numerous media outlets cited the film as a turning point in
Neeson's career that redefined him as an action star.

19
01:21:10,909 --> 01:21:16,909
It also launched a franchise, consisting of two sequels and a television series.

20
01:25:27,272 --> 01:25:33,272
The film explores themes of rescue, paris, france,
kidnapping, prostitution, sex trafficking.

21
01:29:43,636 --> 01:29:49,636
The tone is intense.
